<?xpacket begin="ï»¿" id="W5M0MpCehiHzreSzNTczkc9d"?>
<x:xmpmeta xmlns:x="adobe:ns:meta/" x:xmptk="Adobe XMP Core 5.6-c017 91.164464, 2020/06/15-10:20:05        ">
   <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#">
      <rdf:Description rdf:about=""
            xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"
            xmlns:xmp="http://ns.adobe.com/xap/1.0/"
            xmlns:pdf="http://ns.adobe.com/pdf/1.3/"
            xmlns:xmpMM="http://ns.adobe.com/xap/1.0/mm/">
         <dc:format>application/pdf</dc:format>
         <dc:creator>
            <rdf:Seq>
               <rdf:li>ON Semiconductor</rdf:li>
            </rdf:Seq>
         </dc:creator>
         <dc:title>
            <rdf:Alt>
               <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">Voltage Regulator - Low-Drop 400 mA</rdf:li>
            </rdf:Alt>
         </dc:title>
         <dc:subject>
            <rdf:Bag>
               <rdf:li>The NCV4276C is a 400 mA output current integrated low dropout</rdf:li>
               <rdf:li>regulator family designed for use in harsh automotive environments.</rdf:li>
               <rdf:li>It includes wide operating temperature and input voltage ranges. The</rdf:li>
               <rdf:li>device is offered with 3.3 V</rdf:li>
               <rdf:li>5.0 V</rdf:li>
               <rdf:li>and adjustable voltage versions</rdf:li>
               <rdf:li>available in 2% output voltage accuracy. It has a high peak input</rdf:li>
               <rdf:li>voltage tolerance and reverse input voltage protection. It also</rdf:li>
               <rdf:li>provides overcurrent protection</rdf:li>
               <rdf:li>overtemperature protection and</rdf:li>
               <rdf:li>inhibit for control of the state of the output voltage. The NCV4276C</rdf:li>
               <rdf:li>family is available in DPAK and D2PAK surface mount packages.</rdf:li>
               <rdf:li>The output is stable over a wide output capacitance and ESR range.</rdf:li>
               <rdf:li>The NCV4276C has improved startup behavior during input voltage</rdf:li>
               <rdf:li>transients.</rdf:li>
               <rdf:li>The NCV4276C is pin for pin compatible with NCV4276B.</rdf:li>
            </rdf:Bag>
         </dc:subject>
         <xmp:CreateDate>2019-10-18T14:17:13+08:00</xmp:CreateDate>
         <xmp:CreatorTool>BroadVision, Inc.</xmp:CreatorTool>
         <xmp:ModifyDate>2020-09-01T14:28:28+02:00</xmp:ModifyDate>
         <xmp:MetadataDate>2020-09-01T14:28:28+02:00</xmp:MetadataDate>
         <pdf:Producer>Acrobat Distiller 19.0 (Windows)</pdf:Producer>
         <pdf:Keywords>The NCV4276C is a 400 mA output current integrated low dropout&#xD;&#xA;regulator family designed for use in harsh automotive environments.&#xD;&#xA;It includes wide operating temperature and input voltage ranges. The&#xD;&#xA;device is offered with 3.3 V, 5.0 V, and adjustable voltage versions&#xD;&#xA;available in 2% output voltage accuracy. It has a high peak input&#xD;&#xA;voltage tolerance and reverse input voltage protection. It also&#xD;&#xA;provides overcurrent protection, overtemperature protection and&#xD;&#xA;inhibit for control of the state of the output voltage. The NCV4276C&#xD;&#xA;family is available in DPAK and D2PAK surface mount packages.&#xD;&#xA;The output is stable over a wide output capacitance and ESR range.&#xD;&#xA;The NCV4276C has improved startup behavior during input voltage&#xD;&#xA;transients.&#xD;&#xA;The NCV4276C is pin for pin compatible with NCV4276B.</pdf:Keywords>
         <xmpMM:DocumentID>uuid:af1882a1-6242-40fb-aed4-5c6f3e612e3a</xmpMM:DocumentID>
         <xmpMM:InstanceID>uuid:8b518255-24b1-418d-9856-106ee6073e3b</xmpMM:InstanceID>
      </rdf:Description>
   </rdf:RDF>
